	"notes": "IKEA's homepage opens with a row of category shortcuts (little square icons for Storage, Sofas, Lighting, and so on), then a mosaic of promo tiles: one big tile on the left taller than the rest, with four smaller square deals stacked two-by-two beside it. That mosaic shape — one large tile plus several small ones instead of a plain even grid — is a named layout in this project's own standard (id `4-1`, also called a bento or mosaic grid), and this is a clean real-world example of it. On a phone the mosaic simplifies to just the one big tile, full width, with the smaller deals presumably continuing below it further down the page than our screenshot reaches. The page overall is very long — the scan counts roughly fifteen more full-width sections below the fold that we did not examine one by one.",
